{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>If you afflict, afflict him.</b> It returns to each and every one, whether the orphan or the widow, concerning whom He warned: לא תענון. And the entire language of this verse is doubled, for He doubled the afflicting and the crying out and the hearing." "<b>And it is fitting</b> to interpret in this matter that it is the way of the people of the world, when they are wronged in any matter whatsoever, to seek after saviors and helpers — but the orphan and the widow are weak in strength and have no helpers, and therefore they do not trust in man but only in the Holy One, blessed be He, for He is helper and savior and shield. And because of this the verse makes known that they are helped more than any man, in the manner of what is written concerning them (Proverbs 23:11): ״כי גואלם חזק הוא יריב את ריבם אתך״. And because it is the way of creatures to oppress them constantly all the day, therefore He doubled the afflicting. And it would have been fitting to say 'if you afflict, afflict them,' referring to the orphan and the widow that He mentioned; but He said 'him' to warn not to oppress either one of them time after time — for if one does so, ״כי אם צעוק יצעק אלי״, that is, when either one of them cries out to Me, ״שמוע אשמע צעקתו״ — the cry of each and every one, and likewise every single cry of each one. And therefore the verse needed to double the crying out and the hearing, in order to give hearing for every single cry. And so we find that the degrees of hearing and their ranks correspond to the outcry and the distress that one has in his cry, as it is written (Psalms 39:13): ״שמעה תפלתי ה׳ ושועתי האזינה״ — for prayer, where a man moves his lips, He used the language of 'hearing' (שמיעה); but for a שועה, where one is more distressed and cries out, He used the language of האזנה, which is the inclining of the ear and is greater than 'hearing'; and in the case of tears that come forth from inner humiliation and greater distress, He said ״אל תחרש״, which is the extraction of His will. And you should understand from this how the Holy One, blessed be He, is precise in the pathways of reward, to measure for each one according to his measure." "<b>And similar</b> to this you find in the Midrash on (Job 33:23): ״אם יש עליו מלאך מליץ אחד מני אלף״ — it did not say 'one angel out of a thousand' but 'one מליץ out of a thousand,' that is, one merit out of a thousand liabilities. Or one may say: ״שמוע אשמע צעקתו״ — 'שמוע,' that I will recompense him for the violence that his fellow does to him; 'אשמע,' that I take vengeance upon the one who does the violence to him. And this is ״כי יצעק אלי ושמעתי כי חנון אני״ — and the language of חנינה is the attribute of justice, that is to say, the attribute of justice is stretched out against him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {2 "The citation (איוב ל״ג:כ״ג) is introduced as a Midrash but is in fact Job 33:23; the verse reference itself is correct."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:06.859275543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}